SUMMARY:[Anderson Collection at Stanford University] Patty Chang: surfacin
 g
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T170000
DTSTAMP:20261114T184029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54417960016807-54417960225746@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:\n\nIn surfacing\, Patty Chang engages the ocean
  as a physical\, geopolitical\, and symbolic space\, inviting you to consi
 der the work of collection and recollection. Chang’s multimedia sculptur
 al practice brings together archaeological remains from Point Alones Chine
 se Fishing Village (now the site of Stanford’s Hopkins Marine Station)\,
  fish specimens from Harvard’s Museum of Comparative Zoology\, and archi
 val materials documenting the lives of Chinese fisher families on the Mont
 erey Pen\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://anderson.stanford.edu/exhibiti
 ons/patty-chang-surfacing/\nLast synced: 2026-11-14 10:40 PST
LOCATION:Anderson Collection
URL:https://anderson.stanford.edu/exhibitions/patty-chang-surfacing/
END:VEVENT
