UID:stanford_campus-localist-54481170062431-54481170064480@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Melsa Omaya\, MD\nOncologist and Co-founder of Goodlife Access
 \n\nCervical cancer is preventable\, yet across East Africa\, screening ha
 s stayed out of reach for millions —not for lack of innovation\, but for
  lack of a system that meets patients where they are.\n\nDr. Omaya pioneer
 ed pharmacy-based screening\, proving that early detection doesn't have to
  depend on specialist infrastructure. Join this session to learn why techn
 ological innovation only works when paired with innovation in the system a
 round\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-14 10:40 PST
END:VEVENT
