SUMMARY:[Civil and Environmental Engineering] CEE PhD Defense - Bryam Xavi
 er Astudillo Carpio\, "Assessing practical design methods for strongback b
 raced frames using hazard-consistent collapse risk analysis"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T130000
DTSTAMP:20261114T184029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54313888154549-54313888154550@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: \n\n\nImproving community resilience requires struct
 ural systems that limit structural damage and reduce downtime after an ear
 thquake. Strongback braced frames (SBFs) with buckling-restrained braces (
 BRBs) offer an alternative to more traditional braced frames by reducing d
 rift concentrations. Particularly\, SBFs use a stiff\, essentially elastic
  vertical truss (i.e.\, “strongback”) that redistributes seismic deman
 ds\, enables a more uniform drift distribution\, and mitigates story mecha
 nisms.\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-14 10:40 PST
LOCATION:Y2E2 Building
END:VEVENT
